42059840,Ethical dimensions of artificial intelligence integration into dental practice,10.1016/j.adaj.2026.02.004,,,,,,Chintan Narad; Krishma Sharda; Sakshi Sharma Aasdhir,W7159125004,"Artificial intelligence (AI) is increasingly applied in dentistry to enhance diagnosis and treatment planning. Its integration raises ethical challenges concerning privacy, consent, algorithmic fairness, and professional accountability. The authors synthesized peer-reviewed literature from dental and medical databases. Data were extracted from studies in which researchers addressed ethical principles, legal implications, and regulatory perspectives on AI use in dentistry. Four major ethical domains of autonomy, beneficence, nonmaleficence, and justice were included as central to AI in dentistry. Key concerns include potential bias in algorithms, inequitable technology access, and threats to data confidentiality. The literature supports developing regulatory frameworks and ethical guidelines to ensure safe, fair, and accountable AI implementation in dental settings. Responsible AI integration demands transparency, patient involvement, and ethical literacy among dental care professionals. Establishing governance standards and interdisciplinary dialogue will help preserve trust and fairness in AI-assisted oral health care.",W2968508357; W2972320421; W2989512989; W3016417837; W3046918297; W3164376303; W3165835753; W3200898326; W4225091919; W4311987047; W4327946446; W4378470061; W4385724150; W4385880258; W4391849646; W4394782511; W4400667435; W4409249263; W4413824684,3,2026,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,Asano-original-simplified.csv
28826960,Artificial Intelligence: Threat or Boon to Radiologists?,10.1016/j.jacr.2017.07.007,,,,,,Michael Recht; R. Nick Bryan,W2745394387,"These changes, particularly machine learning/artificial intelligence, will be a boon to radiologists by increasing their value, efficiency, accuracy, and personal satisfaction.",W1997426292; W2044999678; W2069816479; W2165839911; W2493683088; W2520541801; W2523161983; W2525984666; W2558050786,173,2017,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,Asano-original-simplified.csv
41814354,"The potential, perils and pitfalls of Artificial intelligence (AI) in Assisted Reproductive Technologies (ART)",10.1186/s12958-026-01542-z,,,,,,Akanksha Garg; David B. Seifer,W7134911965,"The applications of Artificial intelligence (AI) have exponentially increased in all aspects of life, including within Assisted Reproductive Technologies (ART). Although there is tremendous promise demonstrated by AI assisted tools, there are concerning limitations and cautions to heed before widespread use is adopted into everyday clinical practice. The aim of this review is to offer healthcare providers and researchers an overview of AI applications and to assist them in independently reviewing and appraising AI research in its application to ART.We review different types of AI technologies while exploring current research of applications of AI within ART. Specific applications include embryo and gamete selection and AI as a clinical decision-making support system. We summarize the benefits of integrating AI into an ART setting and describe the known limitations and challenges of this technology in its application to our missions as clinicians, educators and scholars. We consider the ethical implications of AI within ART and equip clinicians and researchers with a framework to critically appraise, evaluate and review research utilizing AI specifically within the setting of ART. We present current international guidance and governance that can be adapted to publishing and reporting AI research in ART.",W2067636960; W2112795664; W2151770813; W2158269238; W2581760718; W2604753693; W2664267452; W2763739959; W2811494171; W2884641698; W2938552295; W2941195539; W2954602225; W2972697612; W2990768863; W3011720571; W3013534864; W3013681994; W3043562073; W3083879023; W3116286104; W3180376856; W4205878348; W4220825947; W4223468055; W4223642954; W4280523108; W4283732597; W4292457666; W4307397047; W4308877642; W4312113558; W4321748226; W4385325894; W4385845014; W4386379644; W4386457977; W4387001850; W4387940598; W4389426448; W4391237786; W4392159936; W4392293571; W4392452791; W4392713662; W4392870093; W4394717747; W4399782760; W4401461817; W4402559330; W4405850664; W4406134571; W4406152330; W4406517998; W4407002549; W4407119846; W4408692262; W4408717517; W4409462597; W4409732831; W4411368489,1,2026,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,Asano-original-simplified.csv
