41176359,Espoirs et risques de l’intelligence artificielle en santé,10.1016/j.spsy.2025.09.005,,,,,,Serge Tisseron,W4415703231,"Artificial intelligence should not only help doctors to better understand diseases and treat them more effectively. It should also enable patients to learn about themselves, make informed decisions about their own health, and integrate their illness into their daily lives. This requires clear ethical guidelines, a good understanding of the challenges of our relationship with machines, the development of caregivers' empathy skills, and the resources necessary for quality care.",W2043002652; W2151186028; W2268165646; W4236521339,0,2025,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,Asano-original-simplified.csv
