32706386,"Clinical, Legal, and Ethical Aspects of Artificial Intelligence-Assisted Conversational Agents in Health Care.",10.1001/jama.2020.2724,,,,,,John D. McGreevey; C. William Hanson; Ross Koppel,W3044211884,,W2099386544; W2293723806; W2623779865; W2843010082; W2946665012,117,2020,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,Asano-original-simplified.csv
38265555,Closing remarks on “The integration and implications of artificial intelligence in forensic science”,10.1007/s12024-024-00785-9,,,,,,Paige Tynan,W4391168860,"This commentary examines the use of artificial intelligence (AI) in forensic science, highlighting its benefits in enhancing accuracy and efficiency across a number of forensic disciplines, including medicine, anthropology, forensics, and taphonomy. However its use, also raises concerns about privacy, data protection, bias, fairness, and the reliability of AI systems. The commentary emphasises the importance of scrutiny, standardized procedures, and ongoing dialogue to ensure AI is responsibly advanced in forensic science.",W4390585076; W4391103648,2,2024,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,Asano-original-simplified.csv
31188116,Digitized Health Opens RWE Floodgates. Can Artificial Intelligence Harness the Power?,,,,,,,,,"Artificial intelligence is creating another new frontier in real-world evidence gathering and analysis. AI's algorithms can approximate-and maybe even surpass-human cognition and judgment in the analysis of complex medical data. Sure, humans will sign off, but AI software will do the heavy lifting.",,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,Asano-original-simplified.csv
