41437470,AI chatbots and scholarly writing,10.1097/NSG.0000000000000279,,,,,,Tina M. Mason; Meagan Blount,W7117157605,"ABSTRACT: Although generative artificial intelligence (AI) chatbots are a promising tool for scholarly writing, caution is needed with hallucinations (incorrect or misleading results). Responsible research design, clear ethical guidelines, and emphasis on authentic scholarly work are critical to ensuring integrity and accurate dissemination. This article examines examples that highlight concerns about accuracy and the necessity of verifying output.",W4221106857; W4318035272; W4365811006; W4376133468; W4386263529; W4388133680; W4389083111; W4389628073; W4390465731; W4392452942; W4392810102; W4393138976; W4395677326; W4398175922,2,2025,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,Asano-original-simplified.csv
