38715069,Generative artificial intelligence is infiltrating peer review process,10.1186/s13054-024-04933-z,,,,,,Kunming Cheng; Zaijie Sun; Xiaojun Liu; Haiyang Wu; Cheng Li,W4396694840,"Table 1 Statement on AI and AI-assisted technologies in peer review in the top ten journals with the highest impact factor in the field of critical care medicine Journals Statement on AI and AI-assisted technologies in peer review Lancet Respiratory Medicine 1. Reviewers should not use artificial intelligence (AI) or AI-assisted technologies to assist in the scientific review of a paper 2. Reviewers should not upload the paper, or any part of it, into an AI tool 3.",W4383371192; W4385659138; W4388288101; W4391508636; W4392781833; W4394923693,36,2024,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,Asano-original-simplified.csv
37307057,Let’s be fair. What about an AI editor?,10.1080/08989621.2023.2223997,,,,,,Xiaoxu Ling; Siyuan Yan,W4380291776,Much of the current attention on artificial intelligence (AI)-based natural language processing (NLP) systems has focused on research ethics and integrity but neglects their roles in the editorial and peer-reviewing process. We argue that the academic community needs to develop and apply a consistent end-to-end policy on the ethics and integrity of NLP in academic publishing: standards such as drafting requirements and disclosure criteria imposed on potential contributors should be consistently applied to the editorial and peer review process in academic publications.,W4318035272,7,2023,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,Asano-original-simplified.csv
34809863,Clinical Application of Artificial Intelligence in Positron Emission Tomography: Imaging of Prostate Cancer,10.1016/j.cpet.2021.09.002,,,,,,Kevin; Stephanie A. Harmon; Ivan S. Klyuzhin; Arman Rahmim; Baris Turkbey,W3214926239,"PET imaging with targeted novel tracers has been commonly used in the clinical management of prostate cancer. The use of artificial intelligence (AI) in PET imaging is a relatively new approach and in this review article, we will review the current trends and categorize the currently available research into the quantification of tumor burden within the organ, evaluation of metastatic disease, and translational/supplemental research which aims to improve other AI research efforts.",W1989888708; W2058426653; W2724500088; W2741135464; W2801867624; W2809848353; W2895593497; W2899740519; W2911471650; W2932791108; W2968974957; W2969238009; W2976273049; W2991901957; W2992749535; W3007566359; W3023993509; W3035869245; W3046865842; W3047319026; W3048516240; W3088047456; W3099824897; W3119494456; W3164816110; W3165803930; W3197578004; W6756046239; W6767289898; W6795158065; W6796194056,14,2022,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,Asano-original-simplified.csv
39040075,A perspective on the artificial intelligence’s transformative role in advancing diffractive optics,10.1016/j.isci.2024.110270,,,,,,Svetlana Nikolaevna Khonina; Nikolay Lvovich Kazanskiy; Albert Efimov; A.V. Nikonorov; Ivan Valer'evich Oseledets; R. V. Skidanov; Muhammad Ali Butt,W4399786316,"Summary Artificial intelligence (AI) is transforming diffractive optics development through its advanced capabilities in design optimization, pattern generation, fabrication enhancement, performance forecasting, and customization. Utilizing AI algorithms like machine learning, generative models, and transformers, researchers can analyze extensive datasets to refine the design of diffractive optical elements (DOEs) tailored to specific applications and performance requirements. AI-driven pattern generation methods enable the creation of intricate and efficient optical structures that manipulate light with exceptional precision. Furthermore, AI optimizes manufacturing processes by fine-tuning fabrication parameters, resulting in higher quality and productivity. AI models also simulate diffractive optics behavior, accelerating design iterations and facilitating rapid prototyping. This integration of AI into diffractive optics holds tremendous potential to revolutionize optical technology applications across diverse sectors, spanning from imaging and sensing to telecommunications and beyond.",W605390931; W619979890; W1637630365; W1970345998; W1976148488; W1982192609; W1989720132; W1990495761; W2008315566; W2011101082; W2021248464; W2049595771; W2070554944; W2079095833; W2087048236; W2090209983; W2096688831; W2142118340; W2294176830; W2800651752; W2900923369; W2922427797; W2947828528; W2965959756; W2990725379; W3016324488; W3031180295; W3041515076; W3048155040; W3082612611; W3087326580; W3092573040; W3096230432; W3103389471; W3120940271; W3128451613; W3144656497; W3178280172; W3184400519; W3190730109; W3195577433; W3201440543; W3202371887; W3203153212; W3216370249; W3217617647; W4210305137; W4210817908; W4210823697; W4212835306; W4221158782; W4245550470; W4281399824; W4283316151; W4283447327; W4283836113; W4313894114; W4317745926; W4320896676; W4360966687; W4362661634; W4362663195; W4378942305; W4386022537; W4386594130; W4387567301; W4387668003; W4389618734; W4390484601; W4390578902; W4391970400; W4393061842; W4395678308; W6603284811; W6627030392; W6630602425; W6642841238; W6777733661; W6785437009; W6798287859; W6800751262; W6850005214; W6850159030; W6853078795; W6853084386; W6860004823; W6861710892,29,2024,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,Asano-original-simplified.csv
39842951,Artificial intelligence in dentistry,10.1016/j.identj.2024.12.004,,,,,,FDI World Dental Federation,W2416397362,"Articial intelligence (AI) has a transformative role in the eld of dentistry. As technology continues to
evolve, AI applications are increasingly integrated into various aspects of dental practice, ranging from
diagnosis and treatment planning to patient management. This review highlights key AI-driven innovations such as image
analysis for radiographic interpretation, predictive analytics for disease risk assessment, and intelligent systems aiding in
treatment customization. The potential impact of AI on enhancing precision, efciency, and overall quality of dental care is
discussed. This article aims to provide a concise overview of the current landscape of AI in dentistry, emphasizing its potential to
reshape and optimize dental healthcare practices.",W4205532368; W4309663439; W4381620840,21,2025,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,Asano-original-simplified.csv
