40662649,Artificial Intelligence Moving Into Respiratory Medicine,10.1111/resp.70093,,,,,,David Chi-Leung Lam,W4412426378,"Artificial Intelligence (AI) has already entered our daily life; we now need to learn to use it in our clinical work.Just like other physicians, respiratory physicians rely on conventional diagnostic and management algorithms to provide optimal care for patients with respiratory diseases.Application of AI tools will be extremely helpful in certain subspecialty situations in Respiratory Medicine.A common example would be the digitalisation of chest x-rays or CT scans where abnormalities are not only detected by AI but can also predict risk of",,0,2025,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,Asano-original-simplified.csv
