35708267,Can artificial intelligence accelerate preclinical drug discovery and precision medicine?,10.1080/17460441.2022.2090540,,,,,,Ali Farnoud; Alexander J. Ohnmacht; Martin Meinel; Michael P. Menden,W4283019716,An average cost of $314 million to $2.8 billion is associated with the development of a new drug with a minimum development period of ten years [1]. The traditional drug discovery process typically...,W1989129581; W1995341919; W1995723686; W2125789330; W2139132031; W2141393790; W2163188200; W2318806991; W2461427403; W2610107437; W2807463161; W2888679364; W2921591500; W2937307539; W2942173509; W2951449549; W2970093742; W3009999522; W3113150977; W3164573547; W3164651207; W4200111709,14,2022,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,Asano-original-simplified.csv
