33417943,Use of Artificial Intelligence in Endoscopic Training: Is Deskilling a Real Fear?,10.1053/j.gastro.2020.12.065,,,,,,Emanuele Sinagra; Francesca Rossi; Dario Raimondo,W3120976773,"We read with interest the study performed by Wang et al1 about the comparation between adenoma miss rates of computer-aided detection colonoscopy versus routine white-light colonoscopy. In this study, the authors concluded that computer-aided detection colonoscopy reduced the overall miss rate of adenomas by endoscopists using white-light endoscopy. Among the limitations of this study, the authors included the fact that only skilled endoscopists were allowed to participate in this study as colonoscopy performers; thus, the results might not be generalizable to junior endoscopists or trainees.",W2738975713; W2981296841; W3036377470; W3087776590,12,2021,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,Asano-original-simplified.csv
