35800112,Editorial: New Frontiers for Artificial Intelligence in Surgical Decision Making and its Organizational Impacts,10.3389/fsurg.2022.933673,,,,,,Lorenzo Cobianchi; Francesca Dal Mas; Luca Ansaloni,W4283208105,"The purpose of the research topic call “New Frontiers for Artificial Intelligence in Surgical Decision Making and its Organizational Impacts “ was to collect the recent developments and undergoing studies in AI in surgery and surgical oncology. More in detail, the aim was to gather contributions on the advancement, deployment, use, and implementation of AI-based applications in surgical practice, understanding their potential contribution to clinical decision making. Moreover, the idea was to assess the potential impacts of such a technology on surgeons, other clinicians, patients, medical institutions, developers, and policy-makers, with an eye open to the organizational and educational consequences and opportunities.",W2944994811; W2995887567; W3148271110; W4213449162; W4221100965; W4224222132; W4224270935; W4281682849; W4281709248,8,2022,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,Asano-original-simplified.csv
