33691975,Artificial intelligence: finding the intersection of predictive modeling and clinical utility,10.1016/j.gie.2020.12.008,,,,,,Karthik Ravi,W3134789991,"Artificial intelligence (AI) refers to the ability of computers to perform tasks normally reserved for human intelligence. AI is a broad concept and encompasses machine learning in which computers use data to create a binary predictive algorithm: deep learning that enhances machine learning by creating algorithms that select and weigh different variables to best predict an outcome. Convoluted neural networks are also created with interconnected “neurons” for pattern recognition, thereby weighing predictive features and learning from the data to predict outcomes.",W1966529893; W2021519563; W2130046526; W2604768315; W2744161219; W2895890926; W2978294504; W3092070069; W4232125274,1,2021,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,Asano-original-simplified.csv
