41903778,Augmenting Medical Education Scholarship Using Artificial Intelligence and Glassick’s Criteria,10.1016/j.acap.2026.103309,,,,,,Scott Moerdler; Suzanne Friedman; Jessica Goldstein; Traci A. Wolbrink,W7141490914,"The emergence of generative artificial intelligence (GenAI) tools, including large language models (LLMs) (eg, ChatGPT, Gemini, Claude), has prompted a reimagining of medical education research and scholarship.1,2 While many educators have embraced GenAI in teaching and learning,3 its potential role in scholarly work remains underutilized. Existing frameworks for evaluating educational scholarship can guide the thoughtful integration of GenAI into medical education research practices.",W4392452942; W4392769984; W4392897370,0,2026,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,Asano-original-simplified.csv
