39103279,[Application and research progress of artificial intelligence in pathological diagnosis of renal cell carcinoma].,10.3760/cma.j.cn112151-20231030-00322,,,,,,Hui Chen; Yuanmei Jiao; Le Qu; Jun Xu; Q Rao,W4401413486,随着人工智能技术的不断发展，病理学领域的人工智能应用也如雨后春笋般涌现。肾细胞癌病理诊断作为其中的应用领域之一，近年来取得了许多重要进展，对临床实践具有指导意义。本文综述了人工智能在肾细胞癌病理诊断中的应用情况及研究进展，并展望未来的研究发展方向。.,,0,2024,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,Asano-original-simplified.csv
38965055,Collective human intelligence vs. artificial intelligence: a comparative analysis for melanoma diagnosis in darker skin tones,10.1111/ijd.17364,,,,,,Noureddine Litaiem; K. Sboui; Jinen Daghrir; Asma Khouladi; Lotfi Tlig; Moez Bouchouicha; Mounir Sayadi; Faten Zéglaoui,W4400339486,could vary in,W1957908168; W3168084226; W4311378251; W4386026199; W4392516399,3,2024,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,Asano-original-simplified.csv
38268783,"Editorial: Recent advances in multimodal artificial intelligence for disease diagnosis, prognosis, and prevention",10.3389/fradi.2023.1349830,,,,,,Hazrat Ali; Zubair Shah; Tanvir Alam; Priyantha D. C. Wijayatunga; Eyad Elyan,W4390699496,"Artificial Intelligence (AI) has gained huge attention in computer-aided decision-making in the healthcare domain. Many novel AI methods have been developed for disease diagnosis and prognosis which may support in the prevention of disease. Most diseases can be cured early and managed better if timely diagnosis is made. The AI models can aid clinical diagnosis; thus, they make the processes more efficient by reducing the workload of physicians, nurses, radiologists, and others. However, the majority of AI methods rely on the use of single-modality data. Other Information Published in: Frontiers in Radiology License: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ See article on publisher's website: https://dx.doi.org/10.3389/fradi.2023.1349830",W4281683654; W4307539314,4,2024,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,Asano-original-simplified.csv
38164494,Editorial: Machine learning-assisted diagnosis and treatment of endocrine-related diseases,10.3389/fendo.2023.1305897,,,,,,Heng Zhang; Ulf D. Kahlert; Wenjie Shi,W4389881865,"Editorial on the Research TopicMachine learning-assisted diagnosis and treatment of endocrine- related diseasesThe endocrine system is an important regulatory system in the human body.It regulates physiological processes such as growth, development, metabolism, and reproduction through the secretion, transfer, and feedback of hormones.Various factors, including environmental, genetic, and lifestyle factors, can lead to the development of endocrine diseases associated with dysfunction of the pituitary, adrenal, and thyroid glands, as well as diabetes.Changes in living environments and lifestyles have led to steady increases in the incidence of endocrine diseases.If not detected and treated in time, these can lead to complications and cause irreversible damage to health.The application of machine learning in medical fields has great prospects (1).This Research Topic is the use of machine learning to establish models for the prediction, diagnosis, and management of endocrine-related diseases for the benefit of both patients and clinical practice.The following is a brief overview of some of the included articles:The model built by Wang et al. using the Gaussian Naive Bayes (GNB) algorithm allows improved prediction of prolonged hospitalization of patients following acute ischemic stroke (AIS).This will assist in policy adjustments for improved resource utilization, thereby alleviating the increasingly heavy economic burden caused by AIS.Chen et al. used a two-sample Mendelian randomization (MR) study to explore the relationship between thyroid function and cholelithiasis.Their findings showed that low-density lipoprotein cholesterol (LDL-C) and apolipoprotein B mediated the effects of FT4 on cholelithiasis risk, with patients with high FT4 levels showing delayed or reduced risk of the long-term effects of cholelithiasis.Zeng et al. analyzed data from the Genomics of Drug Sensitivity in Cancer (GDSC) and The Cancer Genome Atlas (TCGA) databases, using Spearman correlation analysis to identify the key genes that influence Gemcitabine (GEM) efficacy.It was Frontiers in Endocrinology frontiersin.",W2886522935; W4311310219; W4312198046; W4367692580; W4376280052,2,2023,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,Asano-original-simplified.csv
38143924,Editorial: Artificial intelligence applications in chronic ocular diseases,10.3389/fcell.2023.1295850,,,,,,Yanwu Xu; Weihua Yang,W4389434351,"EDITORIAL article Front. Cell Dev. Biol., 07 December 2023Sec. Molecular and Cellular Pathology Volume 11 - 2023 | https://doi.org/10.3389/fcell.2023.1295850",W1972585173; W2083016743; W2782364420; W2800279473; W2897188827; W2979448322; W3041806057; W3093455605; W3101507774; W3136054725; W4221138790; W4223429944; W4281626394; W4288034826; W4289778603; W4323348159; W4386064669; W4386826466,22,2023,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,Asano-original-simplified.csv
38081766,Role of evaluation throughout the life cycle of biomedical and health AI applications,10.1136/bmjhci-2023-100925,,,,,,Edward Hance Shortliffe,W4389801999,"In the development and evaluation of medical artificial intelligence (AI) programmes, there is a tendency to focus the work on the system’s decision-making performance. This is natural, since the typical goal is to develop software that can assist physicians or other clinicians with decision tasks",W3049064638; W3083901094; W3207900783; W4311292456; W4312907108,3,2023,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,Asano-original-simplified.csv
38038952,Leveraging AI to identify dual-purpose aging and disease targets,10.1080/14728222.2023.2288270,,,,,,Geoffrey Ho Duen Leung; Chun Wai Wong; Frank W. Pun; Alex Aliper; Feng Ren; Alex A. Zhavoronkov,W4389221169,"1. Aging is a significant contributor to various chronic diseases, thus emerging as an increasingly important area of research. Elucidating the mechanisms underlying aging can facilitate the develo...",W2007188652; W2010583480; W2119158013; W2125018340; W2142194547; W2144489441; W2399240576; W2415875234; W2770510181; W2954087019; W2975349219; W3211795435; W4220717877; W4229452123; W4289028880; W4292488030; W4313531093; W4313531686; W4315644725; W4322770093; W4367049264; W4380686399; W4384831976; W4386968362; W4387964893,9,2023,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,Asano-original-simplified.csv
