37641487,Ghostwriting: a reflection of academic dishonesty in the artificial intelligence era,10.1093/pubmed/fdad169,,,,,,Raup Padillah,W4386252412,"Dear editors, In this correspondence,1 the authors discuss the various benefits that ChatGPT offers in the educational environment, while also acknowledging the potential dangers it poses to students. . Of particular concern is the issue of academic dishonesty. The advent of artificial intelligence (AI) like ChatGPT has ushered in a new era of possibilities, impact on various aspects, including education. Although AI offers promising tools to enhance learning and streamline academic processes, it also poses challenges to academic integrity. One such challenge is the rise of ‘ghostwriting’—an emerging form of academic dishonesty facilitated by AI-powered language models like ChatGPT. Ghostwriting in an academic context refers to the act of hiring someone else, or in the current case using AI like ChatGPT,2,3 to produce written academic work on behalf of a student. These ghostwriters, powered by advanced AI algorithms, can generate essays, research papers and even dissertations, often without leaving any original thoughts of their involvement. AI language models offer a seemingly convenient and efficient solution, generating custom-written material based on input prompts. When students submit work authored by AI as their own, they misrepresent their abilities and achievements, undermining the fundamental principles of education and fairness. Ghostwriting perpetuates a culture of dishonesty and devalues authentic learning experiences.4",W2213734110; W2491685325; W3147568086; W4292559567; W4293241293; W4321368061; W4362716521; W4377234252; W4381678334; W4384493378; W6854119582; W6854478953,15,2023,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,Asano-original-simplified.csv
