38163479,Artificial Intelligence in Cardiology Research: How to Upskill.,10.1016/j.cjca.2023.12.028,,,,,,Simon Christie; Roger Tam; Zachary Laksman,W4390452853,"As the use of artificial intelligence (AI) in medicine grows, it is imperative for physicians to understand how it can help shape their practice. Whether one wishes to develop novel applications of AI in medicine or become an early-adopter and end-user of AI-based platforms, an in-depth understanding of the capabilities and limitations of AI is crucial. In this brief article, we aim to provide the reader an introduction into machine learning methods, a review of current efforts to integrate AI into cardiology research and clinical implementation, and practical steps for cardiologists and cardiology trainees to begin utilizing these remarkable tools.",W2996061341; W3101609372; W4281606820; W4308144123; W4377965879,2,2024,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,Asano-original-simplified.csv
