42697769,Why pharmacological concepts survive despite scientific progress,10.1016/j.tips.2026.08.008,,,,,,Pierre‐Louis Toutain; Peggy Gandia; Didier Concordet,W7208807456,"Scientific disciplines routinely reassess methods but rarely the concepts guiding scientific reasoning. We identify three mechanisms of conceptual persistence: amnesia, institutionalisation, and reification-the process by which an operational construct is regarded as biological reality. These mechanisms may impede scientific self-correction, a challenge increasingly relevant as artificial intelligence learns from scientific literature.",W144668201; W1892571469; W1993701927; W2039796430; W2060029296; W2132112261; W2158767575; W2898659665; W3032017150; W3209433388; W4323319029; W7140290516,0,2026,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,Asano-original-simplified.csv
