37500505,Trust and confidence of clinical staff and patients is crucial for the successful introduction of artificial intelligence (AI) in mental healthcare,10.1136/ebnurs-2023-103744,,,,,,Alvaro Barrera,W4385302192,"Context This integrative review investigates the evidence for incorporating AIbased DSS in mental healthcare as a partial solution to an escalating care demand which can lead to staff’s burnout and potentially unfinished or missed care. Rightly, the authors of this review mention wider systemic problems such as underresourcing and staff shortages. A DSS is an information system that supports an organisation to make decisions and consist of a knowledge base, a computerised model and user interface. In AI and machine learning (ML) DSS, computers use vast amounts of data to learn underlying patterns, which would not be apparent to a human being, and make predictions based on that data.",W2161374186; W3006635320; W4226049092; W4319293695,1,2024,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,Asano-original-simplified.csv
