38519149,Artificial intelligence-driven cardiac amyloidosis screening,10.1016/S2589-7500(24)00024-4,,,,,,Jacob Abdaem; Robert J.H. Miller,W4393175743,"Transthyretin (ATTR) cardiac amyloidosis is an increasingly recognised disease, especially among older patients with aortic stenosis and heart failure.1 Although the prognosis of patients with ATTR-cardiac amyloidosis is poor without treatment,1 early initiation of targeted therapy reduces all-cause mortality and cardiovascular-related hospitalisations.2 Bone scintigraphy imaging has emerged as a highly accurate method for identifying patients with ATTR-cardiac amyloidosis. However, early identification of patients with ATTR-cardiac amyloidosis remains a clinical challenge, with a median time from symptom onset to diagnosis of 2 years.",W2888036721; W3009897993; W3135050569; W4223416080; W4280494299; W4286499395; W4309337045; W4365139917; W4377966842; W4393021036,2,2024,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,Asano-original-simplified.csv
