38967808,Letter to the Editor of the Journal of Medical Systems: Regarding “Responses of Five Different Artificial Intelligence Chatbots to the Top Searched Queries About Erectile Dysfunction: A Comparative Analysis”,10.1007/s10916-024-02082-y,,,,,,Jakub Brzeziński; Robert T. Olszewski,W4400370126,"Contrary to the article's statement, the authors did not use five different chatbots but four.Interestingly, one of these chatbots underwent a name change during the analysis.The authors failed to provide the specific dates when the chatbots were queried and analyzed, leaving the rationale for counting one chatbot as two unclear.Recent research articles on the utilization of chatbots powered by large language models (LLMs) have noted that Bing has been rebranded as Copilot [3].I am contacting you not to undermine the authors' work but to rectify any inaccuracies.This article might misinform readers interested in utilizing chatbots powered by large language models (LLMs).The authors propose using five distinct chatbots, when in reality, they employ four, as two are identical.",W4393866602; W4394579620,0,2024,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,Asano-original-simplified.csv
38466153,Artificial intelligence tools in medical education beyond Chat Generative Pre-trained Transformer (ChatGPT),10.1093/postmj/qgae014,,,,,,Li Feng Tan; Isaac KS Ng; Desmond Boon Seng Teo,W4392636969,"Dear Editor, Much ink has been spilled on discussing the benefits and risks [1, 2] of artificial intelligence (AI) and specifically Chat Generative Pre-trained Transformer (ChatGPT), which is an AI-powered large language model (LLM) in medical education. From an open letter calling for a moratorium on development of AI systems signed by technology leaders, AI researchers, and entrepreneurs at the end of March 2023 [3], the discourse has evolved to leading academics publishing an editorial in the New England Journal of Medicine (NEJM) AI openly supporting and encouraging the use of LLMs in NEJM AI [4]. We herein summarize the benefits and risks of AI use in clinical training in Table 1. Whilst the focus on AI in medical education has largely been on LLMs, there are many rapidly developing AI tools that are relevant to future healthcare professionals beyond medical curricula and pedagogy. These include AI tools for: A ban on AI in medical education has been acknowledged to not likely be enforceable [4]. Moreover, AI platforms have been rapidly adopted in clinical practice, leading to the emergence of “AI-powered patient care” as a viable health delivery model, which includes AI-guided clinical diagnostics, therapeutic decision-making and prognostication, healthcare administrative assistance, and patient education [5]. It is imperative that medical educators and institutions develop regulation and ethical guidelines on the use of these AI tools in education [6], not just in direct clinical use and training but also in “nonclinical” uses as listed above. Should declarations be made when student presentations are prepared with AI assistance? Should we encourage the use of AI to assist with writing, editing, data analysis, etc. given that these will become increasingly commonplace and even essential skills for future healthcare professionals? It will become increasingly necessary for medical educators to develop skills and agile mindsets to embrace AI technology in medical education, both to optimize its pedagogical utility and to prepare students for real-world practice in AI-assisted clinical environments. Nevertheless, the skills required to thrive as a medical professional [7] such as communication and interpersonal skills, resilience, and self-directed learning certainly remain constant with or without the use of AI in healthcare and beyond. An adaptable mindset that capitalizes on the rapidly evolving landscape of AI tools is necessary and the sooner we engage with AI tools in medical education, the greater the likelihood of success in harnessing its maximal benefit while minimizing its harms.",W4383371446; W4384665085; W4386958277; W4387470302; W4389426432; W6857829565; W6858806741,2,2024,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,Asano-original-simplified.csv
