33328053,Screening for chronic obstructive pulmonary disease with artificial intelligence,10.1016/S2589-7500(20)30076-5,,,,,,Jean‐Emmanuel Bibault; Lei Xing,W3019386492,"The use of artificial intelligence (AI) to perform medical tasks is being assessed in almost every field of practice. Deep neural networks, which were first used to classify pictures of objects, are now being repurposed to diagnose skin cancer,1 screen for breast cancer,2 predict circulatory failure,3 and perform image reconstruction,4 among many other applications. In The Lancet Digital Health, Lisa Y W Tang and colleagues5 report the use of a transfer learning approach to detect signs of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD) on low-dose CT.",W1883683241; W2108307444; W2581082771; W2754103191; W2811374795; W2898753907; W2982067315; W2998175747; W3009583110; W3017504127,20,2020,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,Asano-original-simplified.csv
33148552,Letter to the editor: prediction of survival in colorectal cancer using artificial intelligence,10.1136/gutjnl-2020-323382,,,,,,Ai Guan; Lejia Sun; Meixi Liu; Yilei Mao,W3095192180,"We have read with great interest the article published in Gut by Bibault et al .1 The authors carried out a retrospective study including 154 900 patients from the prostate, lung colorectal and ovarian cancer screening trial to comprehensively train and validate a model to predict survival in colorectal cancer (CRC), using a gradient-boosted machine (GBM). Bibault et al 1 found that physical activity, T stage and tumour grade were the three most critical features among all relevant features. The study showed that the developed model has significant predictive power for survival in patients with CRC. We appreciate their efforts to provide insights into the survival prediction of patients with CRC. However, some points are worthy of further discussion.

First, the essential prognostic factors of patients with CRC, including lymphovascular …",W1513266573; W1591654223; W3011132328; W3083306739,0,2020,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,Asano-original-simplified.csv
