31975516,Artificial intelligence in ophthalmology: Current applications and emerging issues,10.1111/ceo.13716,,,,,,Rachael C. Heath Jeffery; Marcus Smith,W3001338748,"was no madarosis or destruction of lid architecture. An excisional biopsy was performed, revealing histological characteristics consistent with a papillary oncocytoma. The patient underwent further excision with intraoperative frozen-section for an incomplete deep margin with subsequent histology confirming complete excision. Our case is only the 12th reported patient in the literature with an eyelid oncocytoma. This rare, but potentially aggressive tumour has been previously reported to recur despite complete excision in a single case by Morand et al. This case had an unusual presentation of early ptosis and exophthalmos and compounded by the patient's aversion to surgery, ultimately required a right orbital exenteration. In all other cases reported, including ours, the clinical course was much less aggressive, with presentation involving an isolated, usually cystic, eyelid lesion and complete excision being curative (Figure 1). Our case highlights the need to consider rarer tumours in the differential diagnosis when presented with a gradually enlarging cystic lesion on the eyelid and perform biopsywherever suspicious.",W2772246530; W2796849507; W2899431515; W2902963658,1,2020,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,Asano-original-simplified.csv
