42400416,Further Considerations for Objective Facial Paralysis Assessment,10.1097/SCS.0000000000013138,,,,,,Sedat Yaşin; İlhan Bahşi,W7167330262,"This paper discusses the clinical potential of an artificial intelligence-based facial paralysis assessment system. The proposed approach may provide important contributions to the objective evaluation of facial movements and facial symmetry. Several suggestions are presented, including the incorporation of premorbid facial photographs, comparison with established clinical grading systems, and validation in diverse populations. These considerations may further improve the clinical validity, reliability, and generalizability of the proposed method.",W3099302825; W4412073706,0,2026,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,Asano-original-simplified.csv
