35489396,Artificial intelligence for disease diagnosis: the criterion standard challenge,10.1016/j.gie.2022.04.057,,,,,,Yuichi Mori; Masashi Misawa; Jorge Bernal; Michael Bretthauer; Shin‐ei Kudo; Amit Nath Rastogi; Glòria Fernández‐Esparrach,W4224999570,Artificial intelligence (AI) for disease diagnosis is a hot topic. Recent studies have shown that AI tools for computer-aided detection (CADe) of polyps during colonoscopy increases the adenoma detection rate from 19% to 29% with a 50% relative increase.1 The increased detection and removal of the adenomas may lead to increased benefits of screening on the incidence and mortality of colorectal cancer.2,W1988558796; W2008745743; W2051978520; W2914815827; W2916105049; W3001365238; W3035718209; W3036426348; W3087688677; W3130361190; W3156677902; W3161332218; W3189996993; W3211756810; W4223989602,10,2022,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,Asano-original-simplified.csv
