40564376,Artificial Intelligence in Public Health: Bridging Today’s Trends with Tomorrow’s Possibilities,10.3390/bioengineering12060559,,,,,,Daniele Giansanti; Giovanni Costantini,W4410692499,"Driven by the unprecedented challenges of the COVID-19 pandemic, the healthcare sector has witnessed remarkable-and at times sometimes overwhelming-advancements in the role of artificial intelligence (AI) [...].",W3138769367; W3150121917; W3198705930; W3201603287; W3204794075; W4223534709; W4285405102; W4296627002; W4313825605; W4323314501; W4324095540; W4376275035; W4378651670; W4385246972; W4392101274; W4392156369; W4392362010; W4392380411; W4392600753; W4395039528; W4395673789; W4396217572; W4396237723; W4396547560; W4399783795; W4401422727; W4402686627; W4402686717; W4402899191; W4403491386; W4403492613; W4404240393; W4404253935; W4404301731; W4405986655,3,2025,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,Asano-original-simplified.csv
