37417554,"Unleashing the potential: Artificial intelligence in urology for enhanced diagnosis, treatment, and personalized care",10.4111/icu.20230191,,,,,,Garam Lee; Chang Wook Jeong,W4382993042,"Artificial intelligence (AI) has been rapidly changing the world with innovative applications over various domains.Since AlphaGo from Google's DeepMind represented a milestone in developing a super-human level Go program, the release of ChatGPT-3 from OpenAI is proceeding to realize its potential, showing unprecedented performance in handling language-related tasks.The use of deep learning (DL), as a subfield of machine learning (ML), has witnessed striking advances in AI to understand language, images, and speech [1].Recently, ChatGPT has accelerated the development of language models and natural language processing (NLP) applications through the use of the GPT-4 architecture.This generative pre-trained transformer (GPT) architecture allows for continual learning and improvement, as it can be fine-tuned with additional data and feedback.This adaptability has made it a valuable asset in fields such as healthcare, finance, and education, where accurate and efficient communication is essential.In another field, like computer vision, which is the most active domain in DL, AI algorithms have been applied in a wide range of fields.In commerce, AI is used to recognize a customer's facial expression and in-store movements, and analyze those behaviors to provide optimized service.In agriculture, AI improves crop productivity by analyzing aerial images to detect crop health and potential disease outbreaks.In autonomous vehicles, AI enables interpretation and reaction to its surroundings in real-time, ensuring safety and reliability.In manufacturing, AI detects defects or anomalies in products or working environments, allowing for automatic quality control, maintenance, and safety monitoring.From finance, transportation to manufacturing, it is undeniable that AI is driving significant advancements in accuracy, efficiency, and productivity.",W2883667583; W2905810301; W2964273253; W2999399991; W3202230296; W4220886404; W4286633252,9,2023,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,Asano-original-simplified.csv
36967486,"Presidential address: improving item validity and adopting computer-based testing, clinical skills assessments, artificial intelligence, and virtual reality in health professions licensing examinations in Korea",10.3352/jeehp.2023.20.8,,,,,,Hyunjoo Pai,W4360985515,"Progress of health professions licensing examinations in Korea over 31 yearsIn 1992, the Korea Health Personnel Licensing Examination Institute (KHPLEI) was established to provide a national licensing examination system for healthcare professionals [1].Since its inception, the KHPLEI has operated professionally, continuously researching and developing licensing examination systems.By ensuring the minimal competency of healthcare professionals through a stable licensing examination system, the KHPLEI has made significant contributions to the development of healthcare in Korea.Over the past 3 decades, the KHPLEI has undergone significant developments through the dedicated efforts of its former directors, staff, and related organizations.Originally founded as an institute focusing on examinations for medical doctors, the KH-PLEI has been restructured and expanded since 1998.As of 2023, the institution handles licensing examinations for 26 health pro-",W2038973698; W2085760765; W2601075576; W2790391072; W2803637748; W2886253670; W2952037418; W3091133315; W3176679288; W4205748902; W4206537985; W4311668628,2,2023,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,Asano-original-simplified.csv
